{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-424774-r4587448","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Habichuela con Dulce (Dominican Sweet Beans)","sourcePageId":424774,"sourceRevision":"4587448","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-10-26T23:36:07Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Codename Noreste","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Habichuela%20con%20Dulce%20(Dominican%20Sweet%20Beans)&oldid=4587448","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:05:15.620Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Difficult recipes","Category:Dominican recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes using cinnamon stick","Category:Recipes using clove","Category:Recipes using evaporated milk","Category:Recipes using granulated sugar","Category:Recipes using kidney bean","Category:Recipes using sweet potato","Category:Recipes using sweetened condensed milk","Category:Recipes with images"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"9cf65b8edbe999c44f38db0e6c544968fd310aef1bd2b3dfae4ad26de514893f","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Name = Habichuela con Dulce\n| Servings = 10+\n| Difficulty = 4\n| Image = [[File:Habichuela con dulce.png|300px]]\n| Category = Recipes for dessert\n| Time = 1 hr 5 mins\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''''Habichuela con dulce''''', also known as sweet beans or sweet cream of beans is a Dominican [[Cookbook:Dessert|dessert]] that is mostly made during Good Friday.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] soft-boiled red [[Cookbook:Kidney Bean|kidney beans]]\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Raisin|raisins]]\n\n* 3 cups [[Cookbook:Condensed Milk|evaporated milk]]\n\n* 2 cups [[Cookbook:Sweetened Condensed Milk|sweetened condensed milk]]\n\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] salt (or 1 pinch)\n* 1 cup granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 1 tsp [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla]] extract\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]] sticks\n* 10 [[Cookbook:Clove|cloves]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Sweet Potato|sweet potato]] (batata), cubed small\n* Milk cookies\n\n== Procedure ==\n# Blend cooked beans, including the water they cooked in, into a purée.\n# Strain beans into a pot in order to get rid of any skins.\n# Mix in sweetened condensed milk, evaporated milk, vanilla extract, salt, sugar, sweet potatoes, cinnamon sticks, and cloves.\n# Simmer over low heat until the sweet potatoes are fully cooked. Stir occasionally so that it will not stick on the bottom.\n# Add raisins and [[Cookbook:Simmering|simmer]] for 10 minutes. You can also add the milk cookies if you want them to become soft.\n# Remove beans from heat.\n# If you want, you may remove the cinnamon sticks and cloves.\n# Serve beans in a bowl, and add milk cookies on top. You may serve warm or chilled.\n\n[[Category:Dominican recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes using kidney bean]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sweet potato]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cinnamon stick]]\n[[Category:Recipes using clove]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sweetened condensed milk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using evaporated milk]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Habichuela con Dulce (Dominican Sweet Beans)","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"10+","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"4 cups soft-boiled red kidney beans","sourceTex